const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"预测精度与变量选择是两个目标",en:"Prediction and variable selection are distinct goals"},body:{zh:"Zou与Hastie从预测误差和模型简洁性两方面讨论回归。Lasso能够产生零系数，但面对强相关变量或变量多于观测的情形会有局限；弹性网尝试在稀疏选择中保留相关变量的信息，不是宣称所有数据都优于其他方法。",en:"Zou and Hastie consider predictive error and parsimony separately. Lasso produces zero coefficients but can struggle with correlated predictors or more predictors than observations. Elastic net seeks sparse selection while retaining information shared by correlated variables; it is not universally superior."},reference:{url:"https://hastie.su.domains/Papers/elasticnet.pdf",label:{zh:"2004年8月修订稿 · §1",en:"August 2004 revision · §1"}}},{title:{zh:"标准化属于模型定义",en:"Standardization belongs to the model definition"},body:{zh:"文中先将响应变量中心化，并令每个预测变量均值为零、平方和为一。惩罚施加在系数上，因此改变变量单位会改变惩罚的相对作用。编辑建议记录训练期的中心与尺度，应用到后续样本时不能重新借用未来数据估计。",en:"The manuscript centers the response and gives each predictor zero mean and unit sum of squares. Since penalties act on coefficients, measurement units affect their relative influence. Editorial application: retain training-period centers and scales rather than estimating preprocessing from future observations."},reference:{url:"https://hastie.su.domains/Papers/elasticnet.pdf",label:{zh:"2004年8月修订稿 · §2.1",en:"August 2004 revision · §2.1"}}},{title:{zh:"两个惩罚，不要只对照参数名",en:"Two penalties, not just a familiar parameter name"},body:{zh:"最初的目标函数把残差平方和、L1惩罚与平方L2惩罚相加。该稿用两个惩罚系数定义混合比例，比例为一对应岭回归、为零对应Lasso。软件中的同名参数未必沿用这个方向，应对照目标函数而不是直接复制数字。",en:"The initial objective combines residual sum of squares, an L1 penalty and a squared L2 penalty. Its mixing convention assigns one to ridge and zero to lasso. A software parameter with the same name need not follow that convention; compare objective functions rather than copying values."},reference:{url:"https://hastie.su.domains/Papers/elasticnet.pdf",label:{zh:"2004年8月修订稿 · §2.1",en:"August 2004 revision · §2.1"}}},{title:{zh:"相关变量的成组效应",en:"Correlated variables can move together"},body:{zh:"平方L2部分使目标更严格地凸化，并鼓励高度相关变量取得相近的系数。这里的成组效应来自变量之间的相关结构，不要求事先给出行业或特征分组；它也不等于研究者已经识别出具有经济含义的独立因素。",en:"The squared L2 component strengthens convexity and encourages highly correlated predictors to receive similar coefficients. This grouping effect arises from their correlation, without a predefined sector or feature group. It does not establish that the selected variables are independent economic mechanisms."},reference:{url:"https://hastie.su.domains/Papers/elasticnet.pdf",label:{zh:"2004年8月修订稿 · §2.3–2.4",en:"August 2004 revision · §2.3–2.4"}}},{title:{zh:"原文区分朴素估计与修正估计",en:"The original paper distinguishes naive and corrected estimates"},body:{zh:"作者指出两个惩罚可能带来双重收缩，并将修正估计写成朴素估计的重缩放：乘以一加L2惩罚系数。这个关系依赖该稿的标准化与目标函数定义。阅读复现代码时，应先确认实现的是哪一种估计，不能额外重复修正。",en:"The authors identify double shrinkage and rescale the naive estimate by one plus the L2 penalty coefficient. That relation depends on the manuscript's normalization and objective. Before interpreting replication code, establish which estimator it implements; do not apply the correction twice."},reference:{url:"https://hastie.su.domains/Papers/elasticnet.pdf",label:{zh:"2004年8月修订稿 · §3.1–3.2 · p. 10",en:"August 2004 revision · §3.1–3.2 · p. 10"}}},{title:{zh:"方法有效不等于样本外收益有效",en:"An estimator is not evidence of an investable forecast"},body:{zh:"这篇文章讨论统计估计与变量选择，而不是为某个金融因子组合提供收益承诺。编辑建议将调参、变量筛选、预处理和最终评价分开，并保留按时间划分的未用样本；相关变量被一同保留，也不构成因果识别。",en:"The article studies estimation and selection, not promised returns from a financial signal. Editorial application: separate tuning, feature selection, preprocessing and final evaluation, with untouched chronological observations. Retaining correlated variables together also does not identify causation."},reference:{url:"https://hastie.su.domains/Papers/elasticnet.pdf",label:{zh:"2004年8月修订稿 · §1; §3.2",en:"August 2004 revision · §1; §3.2"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"导读依据2004年修订稿，正式期刊引用不变。弹性网是一种估计方法，不保证金融预测有效；参数名称、损失函数缩放和原文的重缩放定义需分别核对。",en:"This guide uses the 2004 revision, separately from the journal citation. Elastic net does not guarantee useful financial forecasts. Parameter names, loss scaling and the original rescaling definition must be checked separately."}};export{e as default};
